abstract: >-
  BioReview-Bench is a silver-standard benchmark for measuring overlap with
  concerns recorded in published biomedical peer review. The public release is
  a rights-minimized index containing text-free metadata for 6,940 articles and
  categorical train/validation labels; publisher prose and test targets are not
  redistributed. The complete local benchmark contains 101,869 normalized
  concern records from eLife, F1000Research, PLOS, PeerJ, and Nature Portfolio.
